The Range Rover Sport P460e is a plug-in hybrid variant introduced on the L461 generation from 2022. It combines a 3.0-litre inline-six petrol engine with an electric motor, delivering 460PS of combined output. The P460e shares its AJ300 powertrain architecture with the P440e PHEV variant, with a higher power tune. As the L461-generation Range Rover Sport continues in production, the P460e remains a current variant across the latest model years.

Land Rover Range Rover Sport P460e Engine Compatibility
The P460e uses the AJ300 PHEV powertrain — a 3.0-litre inline-six petrol engine paired with an electric motor and battery pack. Because the PHEV system integrates engine and electric drivetrain components, compatibility is specific to the L461 chassis generation. Before we quote or supply anything, we confirm:

Your exact engine and PHEV specification via registration or VIN

Your generation (L461)

Drivetrain and ancillary specification

Any electronics or ECU considerations specific to your exact build

This is why we always start with your registration rather than a generic quote — it protects you from paying for parts that don't fit your actual car.

