Frequently Asked Questions
What engine does the Land Rover Range Rover Sport P460e use?
The P460e uses the AJ300 PHEV — a 3.0-litre inline-six petrol engine paired with an electric motor, producing 460PS of combined output.

How much does a Land Rover Range Rover Sport P460e engine rebuild cost?
Rebuilds start from £3,200. Exact price depends on condition and parts required — submit your reg for a fixed-price quote.

Which engine code is fitted to my Range Rover Sport P460e?
The Range Rover Sport P460e uses the AJ300 PHEV engine code. Enter your registration on this page and we'll confirm your exact spec before you're quoted anything.

Do you rebuild AJ300 PHEV Range Rover Sport P460e engines?
Yes. We replace timing chains, bearings and gaskets as standard on every AJ300 PHEV rebuild.

Do you supply used Range Rover Sport P460e engines?
Yes, in some cases a matched low-mileage used engine is the right option. Our team will advise honestly once we've matched your registration and understood your situation.

Can you recover my Range Rover Sport P460e if the engine has failed?
Yes — nationwide recovery is available from £70, and most vehicles are collected within a few hours of booking.

How long does a Range Rover Sport P460e engine rebuild take?
Most rebuilds are completed within 3-5 working days from the time your car arrives at our workshop.

Is rebuilding better than fitting a used engine?
For most Range Rover Sport owners, yes. A rebuild removes the compatibility risk that comes with an unknown used unit's history, and comes with a 12-month unlimited-mileage warranty — often longer and more comprehensive than what a used engine supplier offers.

